- introduce `property.Schemas`, `property.Values`, `property.Properties` and `crypto.Properties`.
    + `property.Schemas` is used to replace the `types.ModuleVariable`, `types.ModuleOutput` and `types.ApplicationVariable`, it is an array of `property.Schema`.
        ```
        [
          {
            "name": "string",
            "description": "string",
            "type": <explain later>,
            "default": <you can put anything here, object/slice/string/bool/...>,
            "required": true,
            "sensitive": true,
            "label": "string",
            "group": "string",
            "options": [
              "string"
            ],
            "showIf": "string",
            "hidden": true
          },
          ...
        ]
        ```
    + `property.Values` is used to replace the `map[string]interface{}`, in fact, we do not need to encode/decode the input variables/attributes twice, we save what the user typed and encode/decode when we need. `property.Values` can work with `property.Schemas` to validate input content whether matches the specified type(module version schema).
    + `property.Properties` describes the type of value itself. `crypto.Properties` is similar to `property.Properties`, but the user can leverage a `visible: false` to erase the value during outputting.
        ```
        {
            "type": "<explain later>",
            "value": <you can put anything here, object/slice/string/bool/...>,
            "visible": true/false,
        }
        ```

